# no-network-egress.inv — trading-binance is backtest-only (#1737): no
# variant may reach the network at all. Capability-absence (v3,
# agentis-core #943): `forbidden_callee_used` is true iff the candidate
# statically calls any of the listed callees, regardless of arguments.
#
# Deliberately NOT expressed as egress_allow/egress_outside_allowlist (the
# docs' own api.binance.com / data.binance.vision example). Verified live
# against the installed v1.26.0 binary and the real strategist.ag sources
# that an egress-allowlist module ALWAYS culls the legitimate strategist:
#   (a) strategist.ag uses `exec sh` throughout for legitimate local-only
#       work (env reads, timestamps, invoking tools/verify-trade.sh) — any
#       `exec` is unconditionally opaque under the v3 predicate, and
#   (b) independent of (a), the legitimate `replicate(target_r, ...)` call
#       passes a non-literal, memo-derived `target_r`
#       (`select_replication_target()` never returns a literal), and
#       `replicate`'s host-arg is itself a covered egress channel
#       (agentis-core #948) — also opaque.
# So copying the documented egress-allowlist example verbatim would be a
# self-inflicted permanent cull of the incumbent, not a useful law. Instead
# this module denies the network-capable CALLEES by name: `http_get` /
# `http_post` cover direct HTTP egress, `use_tool` covers dispatch through
# the tool-invocation surface (a literal tool name is recorded as both an
# egress destination and a callee, so this also catches
# `use_tool("place_order", ...)`-style dispatch), and `smtp_send` covers the
# one network builtin the egress-allowlist predicate does not itself
# inspect (agentis-core config-reference.md #943 coverage boundary).
#
# None of these callees exist anywhere in any of the six
# `tribe-*/agents/strategist.ag` today (verified by grep and by
# `agentis invariant check` returning decision:"pass" for all six against
# this module) — trading-binance's only network-capable code lives in
# host-side Python tools that run BEFORE daemon spawn, never inside `.ag`.
class = inviolable
forbidden_callee = http_get
forbidden_callee = http_post
forbidden_callee = use_tool
forbidden_callee = smtp_send
when forbidden_callee_used == true
